Troubleshooting
Issue: Import errors for versioning_utils

Ensure versioning_utils.py is in the same directory as app.py
Check that you've implemented all required functions
Issue: 404 errors on API calls

Verify Flask app is running: ps aux | grep python3
Check that routes are registered: Look for route definitions in app startup logs
Ensure correct URL format: /api/v1/users not /api/v1/users/
Issue: JSON parsing errors

Verify Content-Type header: -H "Content-Type: application/json"
Check JSON syntax in curl commands
Use single quotes around JSON data in curl
Issue: Deprecation headers not appearing

Ensure decorator is applied before route decorator
Check that make_response() is used to create response object
Verify headers are set before returning response
Conclusion
In this lab, you implemented API versioning using URL path-based versioning strategy. You created two versions of a user management API, where v1 provides basic functionality and v2 adds enhanced features while maintaining backward compatibility with v1.

Key accomplishments:

Designed versioned routes using /api/v1/ and /api/v2/ patterns
Implemented version-specific business logic and response formats
Added deprecation warnings to older API versions
Maintained backward compatibility allowing both versions to coexist
Created utilities for version management and routing
This approach allows you to evolve APIs without breaking existing client integrations, a critical skill for production API development.
